# Accepted, documented vulnerability exceptions for the Trivy CI gate.
# The non-blocking "Trivy report" step does NOT use this file, so these still
# show up in CI logs for visibility.

# CVE-2025-68121 — Go stdlib crypto/tls: incorrect certificate validation during
# TLS session resumption. Present in the upstream dnsx/naabu Go binaries (compiled
# with Go < 1.24.13). We already pin the latest available releases (dnsx 1.2.3,
# naabu 2.6.1); no fixed tool release exists yet. Out of our control until
# ProjectDiscovery rebuilds with patched Go — revisit and bump the pins then.
CVE-2025-68121

# GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw — github.com/getkin/kin-openapi: ValidationHandler.Load()
# fail-open auth bypass via NoopAuthenticationFunc default, fixed in kin-openapi
# 0.144.0. Pulled in transitively by nuclei's go.mod (still pinned to 0.132.0 as
# of the latest tagged release, v3.11.0 — the fix landed on nuclei's dev branch
# but hasn't shipped in a release yet). Not exploitable here: nuclei only imports
# kin-openapi's openapi3/openapi3gen packages to parse target OpenAPI/Swagger
# specs for its input format (pkg/input/formats/openapi, pkg/input/formats/swagger)
# — it never constructs an openapi3filter.ValidationHandler, so the vulnerable
# fail-open code path is unreachable in this binary. Revisit once ProjectDiscovery
# ships a nuclei release with kin-openapi >= 0.144.0.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw
